    "body": "Work is on `issue/2014-tool-property-grid-v2` in the worktree\n`.claude/worktrees/issue-2014-v2`, at head `97f6cb595`. The orchestrator\ngates and pushes it.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- The tool page in Properties draws each setting as one row. The label\n  stands in the left half and the input in the right half. The rows are\n  in four collapsible groups: Geometry, Holder, Cutting data, Catalog.\n- The grid is in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings_grid.rs`. The page,\n  the three columns and the Apply / Add commands stay in\n  `tool_settings.rs`.\n- The inline help text is now a hover tooltip on the row label.\n- The per-material table scrolls across inside Cutting data. It no longer\n  widens the page or the tool editor window.\n- A group title folds its group, as its arrow does.\n- Each edit still goes through one undoable `ChangeTool` command. The\n  Apply and undo test is unchanged and green.\n- No snapshot PNG changes. The modal `tool_editor_window` stays; #2003\n  retires it.\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `egui_app::tests::structural::tool_properties::tool_settings_form_a_label_left_grid_in_collapsible_groups`\n  fails before the change: it checks the four group titles, each group's\n  rows, the label left of its input on one row, and that Holder folds and\n  unfolds.\n- `egui_app::tests::page_layout::layout_page_tool` names the Geometry\n  header with the rows under it.\n- The #2002, waterjet, ball-nose and tool-editor tests now read the\n  label-left layout. They still guard the same behaviour.\n\nResults: the `camcraft-ui` lib suite is green with `--test-threads=4`:\n1171 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui\n--all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nNot exercised: I did not take screenshots. The PR needs a before and\nafter screenshot of the Properties tool page, as the issue asks.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
